> nice to be able to pick and choose packages as well. I find these unit
> install options (Kde, Gnome, Wkstation etc) to be madding.

Hello;

Someone already recommended Debian, so I'll second that.=20

Give Debian GNU/Linux a try. The inital install may be slightly more
time consuming then say RatHat, but it's well worth it IMO! I believe
the base install for the lastest release of Debian GNU/Linux is less
then 50MB. After you have a base install completed you can then
configure 'apt' for your local/favorite mirror. 'apt' can then install
whatever package(s) you want as well as remove those you don't.=20

I recommend subscribing to both debian-user and debian-alpha mail lists:=20

Send mail to "debian-user-request@lists.debian.org" (with subscribe in=20
the body). This list is excellent for general Debian and Linux issues.=20
If you need to know something that is not platform specific, you ask=20
here. There is also a digest version of this list (it is high traffic).
just send your email to "debian-user-digest-request@lists.debian.org"
instead of the address above.=20

Send mail to "debian-alpha-request@lists.debian.org" (with subscribe in=20
the body). This is list is for debian on alpha. If you have a question=20
about something specific to debian on alpha, here is the place.=20

When installing you will be asked to define a configuration for your
system (i.e. workstation, server, etc) just select the base install
option.=20

If you require help installing, feel free to contact me.=20

HTH,
Ron
